WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.220
Good morning Hank.

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:02.220
It's Tuesday.

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:05.000
Let me take this gauze out of my mouth.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Oh God.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.090
I just had a pretty invasive oral surgery
down here Hank.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.090
Uh...

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:13.190
This is definitely the highest I've ever been
when making a vlogbrothers video.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.450
My mouth hurts so bad.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:19.070
Hank, do you know the first time that I reference
this pain that I still have was in my second

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:21.500
vlogbrothers video in 2007.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.140
Hank as you know, I had surgery on my mouth
a few weeks ago.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:29.019
After they sewed my gum back into my mouth,
my mouth tasted like cement and blood and

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:30.029
burnt meat.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:33.530
This is the 4th and most dramatic surgery
that I've had and I gotta say that I have

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:34.530
great care.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:35.530
I have a great oral surgeon.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:36.530
Great dentist.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.210
So I really am confident that this is finally
going to work.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.710
But ugh chronic pain is just the worst.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:45.069
The thing about physical pain Hank, is that
it's almost inexpressible.

00:00:45.069 --> 00:00:49.729
Like, uh, there's this great book, "The Body
in Pain" by Elaine Scary, that talks about

00:00:49.729 --> 00:00:55.109
how like, pain doesn't just defy language,
it kind of destroys language.

00:00:55.109 --> 00:00:58.109
Like it's just impossible to use language
to get other people to understand what your

00:00:58.109 --> 00:01:01.989
physical pain is like because your physical
pain is always only yours.

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:06.820
But anyway, Hank, this particular surgery
was necessitated because a metal rod had emerged

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:12.990
from out of my gum, erupting from the skin
and pressing against my lip.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:16.200
That's the best that I can do to use language
to describe how much it hurt.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.719
Hank I'm sorry this video isn't funnier.

00:01:17.719 --> 00:01:20.570
Oh, is that- oh it's dried blood.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:21.570
That's nice.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:22.609
That's a nice look for today.

00:01:22.609 --> 00:01:26.520
But anyway Hank, in the last twenty four hours
I've been thinking a lot about how lucky I

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.520
am.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.720
Like I have access to the best oral surgeons
and the best dentists, so you know this suffering

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.390
is just necessary.

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:35.320
But there's a lot of suffering that's completely
unnecessary and my favorite thing about the

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.570
Nerdfighter community is that we try to do
stuff about that.

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.630
So anyway thinking about that let me just
start a fundraiser over at Save the Children

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:44.270
to help them out with their work with Syrian
refugees.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:48.140
Save the Children is doing amazing work to
get kids in refugee camps access to healthcare

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.909
and education and nutrition.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:53.539
So yeah I started a fundraiser called Nerdfighters
Opposed to Human Suffering Including but not

00:01:53.539 --> 00:02:00.039
Limited to John's Post-Operative Pain, which
a Nerdfighter on Tumblr helpfully shortened

00:02:00.039 --> 00:02:04.259
to NOHSIbnLtJPOP, or as I like to call it
"No Sea Bin Lieutenant J-Pop."

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:08.190
Nerdfighters I will match all your donations
up to $20,000 and I'm not just saying that

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:12.730
because I'm high, I asked Sarah earlier if
it was O.K. and she said yes.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:15.890
Hank the only thing I can really say about
pain is that it sucks.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:19.069
I don't think that it's romantic or transcendent
or any of that.

00:02:19.069 --> 00:02:20.599
I think it just sucks.

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:23.250
And I think where we can help alleviate it,
we should.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:24.250
So donate if you can.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:25.980
If not to this fundraiser then to another.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.540
And of course it's O.K. if you can't donate
as well.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.099
You've gotta take care of yourself.

00:02:30.099 --> 00:02:32.819
Alice needs me to read her an Elmo story so
I gotta go, Hank.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:33.879
I'll see you on Friday.

